Nursing Note 7p-7a:
NUrsing Assessment;

Pt is pleasant and cooperative and orientated to person, place, and time. Afebrile. HCt 24, transfused with 2 units prbcs. Post hct pending. Moves all extremities and turns with minimal assist. HR nsr 70-80 and received scheduled 10mg ivpb lopressor for beta blockade. JP continues to put out approximately 20-30cc/hr of serous drainage, sample. Abdomen soft and pt states positive flatus. drinking sips of water and tolerating well. Remains on insulin gtt. Emotional support. Pleaser refer to carevue for details.

CSRU Nursing 7p-7a
Neuro: alert and oriented x3; little sleep overnight; no deficits noted; Restless @ times- refused some treatments and meds saying "I don't need that"
CV: Sinus rhythm 70-80's; Hypertensive during evening, however BP improved w/ increase in metoprolol dosage; Skin warm and dry; Pulses palpable;
Resp: 2 L NC; Sats 94-96% (only 89% when tried RA); Lungs clear, diminished bases bilat; Resps nl; weak cough; Refuses IS; CT in place, no leak noted;
GI: Abd soft, nondistended; hypoactive bowel sounds; denies nausea;
GU: Foley in place; urine clear, yellow-adequate output-on lasix [**Hospital1 **]
Skin: Sternal incision covered by tegaderm; No breakdown noted
Activity: OOB w/ assist x2 this am;
Pain: Mso4 given for pain-refused percocet; adequate pain relief w/meds
Plan: D/C central line and aline; cont activity; transfer to floor

npn 7p-7a

dx: end stage myelodysplastic syndrome w/ pancytopenia; sepsis;

neuro:
pt lethargic, weak, PERL; moves left arm up toward face--unclear if to scratch psoriasis or attempt to remove face mask;

c-v:
remains on low dose dopamine; also natrecor--urine output approx 80+ mls/hr;
   no ectopy observed this night;
   b/p adequate, hypertensive when faceial cpap applied;
   has generalized edema which natrecor is attempt to diurese off;
new hrt murmur as of yesterday, therefore ordered for echo--likely d/t total body fluid accumulation d/t kidney failure;
   received 20 meq KCL for 18:00 serum K+ 3.4; this a.m. serum K+ 4.0;

heme:
continues to have worsening pancytopenis; this a.m.'s plt ct 21;

resp:
O2 sat 100% when on facial cpap; approx 93-95% when on nc 4-5 l plus face tent;
   lungs coarse bilat;
   facial bipap applied for about 3 hours, from 12a-3a d/t accessory muscles used for breathing (shoulders, abdominal);facial cpap dc'd after 3 hours d/t hypertension (sbp 180's); sbp down to 146 after facial cpap removed and pt given additional morphine sulfate;


g-i:
started on TPN yesterday evening; pt peviously on insulin gtt; anticipate pt will need increased in insulin needs again d/t TPN and steroids;
   fecal incontinence bag applied yesterday, using duoderm to protect pts already fragile skin;

g-u:
pt w/ increasing creatinine--2.9; natrecor effective in assisting urine output;

skin:
pt w/ scattered bruises, psoriasis, bleeds easily d/t pancytopenia; has scattered DSD's for these abrasions;
   steroid cream applied to psoriasis lesions;

comfort;
