plan of care per team and HCP

Nursing Note 7a-7p:
Nursing Assessment;

Tmax 99, 98-97 for majority of shift. WBC 13. Sputum sent. Pt requiring ativan prn for anxiety and morphine prn for pain. [**Name (NI) 103**] wife in to visit and pt much calmer in her presence. Lungs clear to coarse and suctioned occasionally for some tan thick secretions. Albuteral and atrovent given by respiratory. [**Name (NI) **] [**Name (NI) 657**] and flap ruddy and pink. Tube feeds remained on hold from prior emesis during night and for probable OR. To OR at 1830 for wound washout. Emotional support provided. Please refer to carevue for details.

npn 01:30-07:00 (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: resp failure

